<p class="chips"><span class="chip">MIT license</span><span class="chip">Model-agnostic</span></p>
</div>
<div class="project-body">
<p class="eyebrow">Project 01</p>
<h2 class="h-lg">WikiSage</h2>
<p class="subhead">Context-Aware AI Knowledge Integration</p>
<blockquote class="pull">
<p class="label">Friction</p>
<p class="pull-text">Traditional knowledge management systems lack dynamic, context-aware AI synthesis that respects private data structures and modular user workflows.</p>
</blockquote>
<div class="rows">
<div class="row">
<p class="row-label">Response</p>
<p class="row-text">Built WikiSage, an open-source companion plugin supporting multi-model architectures (Claude, OpenAI, Gemini, Ollama) to process rich document types, manage history, and execute smart operations inside user wikis.</p>
</div>
<div class="row">
<p class="row-label">Innovation</p>
<p class="row-text">Model-agnostic integration of LLMs within TiddlyWiki knowledge bases, working from structured metadata and retrieval-based approaches.</p>
</div>
</div>
<details class="more"><summary>What the README lists, and the guardrails</summary><ul><li>Multi-model support</li><li>PDF analysis and processing</li><li>Image generation and handling</li><li>Voice interaction (speech-to-text and text-to-speech)</li><li>Smart content editing with macros</li><li>Context-aware wiki operations</li><li>Conversation history management</li><li>Intelligent search and navigation</li></ul><p>Guardrails: the agent cannot delete tiddlers directly, and its edits can be undone. The README still recommends keeping backups.</p></details>
<p class="links">
<a class="btn" href="https://github.com/well-noted/WikiSage" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/well-noted/WikiSage</a>
<a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://well-noted.github.io/WikiSage/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Live demo</a>
</p>
</div>
</article>

<article class="project flip wrap" id="logos">
<div class="project-art">
<div class="logo-tile"><$image source="Logo/Logos" alt="Logos logo"/></div>
<p class="tile-cap">Desktop app, written in Rust</p>
<p class="chips"><span class="chip">v0.0.0</span><span class="chip">Under active development</span><span class="chip">Tested on Windows so far</span></p>
</div>
<div class="project-body">
<p class="eyebrow">Project 02</p>
<h2 class="h-lg">Logos</h2>
<p class="subhead">An Agent-Based Modeling Environment</p>
<blockquote class="pull">
<p class="label">Friction</p>
<p class="pull-text">Legacy modeling platforms like NetLogo have a steep syntax learning curve and an isolated execution model that limits dynamic rule generation.</p>
</blockquote>
<div class="rows">
<div class="row">
<p class="row-label">Response</p>
<p class="row-text">Engineered Logos, an environment that reads and writes NetLogo's .nlogox format without loss and runs models on the real NetLogo engine, so a teaching model can grow into a research study without being rewritten, for exploratory socio-ecological simulations.<!-- Restore once the AI features are pushed: adding native AI-driven logic and modular agent behaviors. --></p>
</div>
<div class="row">
<p class="row-label">Testing &amp; Iteration</p>
<p class="row-text">Built through a rigorous development lifecycle featuring continuous validation, extensive testing of agent interaction networks, and proactive resolution of syntax edge cases.</p>
</div>
</div>
<details class="more"><summary>What the README lists</summary><ul><li>Model screen with Interface, Info, and Code tabs, using NetLogo's own view rendering</li><li>Code editor with diagnostics, completion, and rename from NetLogo's compiler through a language server</li><li>Interface editing with a single undo history</li><li>Agent inspection, watches, and a Command Center</li><li>BehaviorSpace experiments run in parallel, with results as NetLogo-compatible tables or Parquet</li><li>Search and replace across code, Info, and widgets</li><li>Project files that list data, Python requirements, and secret names, with secrets kept in the OS credential store</li><li>Autosave every 30 seconds and crash restore</li><li>A command-line tool to run and check models without the app</li></ul><p>Requires NetLogo 7.0.4, installed separately. The README states that Logos is usable but under active development.</p></details>
<p class="links">
<a class="btn" href="https://github.com/well-noted/Logos" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/well-noted/Logos</a>
</p>
</div>
</article>

